Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:19:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: discharge eleven REGISTRATION OWED rows, and
 close two live holes in the guard itself

The protected-win baseline carried fourteen rows marked REGISTRATION OWED - real, landed wins
whose manifest entry could not yet be written without inventing a field. Eleven of them are now
written. Three are not, and they stay owed with the exact missing measurement named.

REGISTERED (eleven baseline rows, ten entries):
  4672638cf                powerinfer-windows-port-avx-cure      (subtree `powerinfer` + the flag)
  655f2f9a3                powerinfer-expert-bundle-generator
  11c9a7702                powerinfer-streamed-repack-carveout
  bca0f5b9a                powerinfer-gpu-safe-staging
  bf0abf0be + 39a585bd5    rocmfpx-weight-formats                (one guard, one capability)
  e44c0bb0d                cpu-vnni-repack-default-off
  e20a8df7f -> e96d7484a   cpu-vnni-repack-g128-kernels          (the kernel, per e20a8df7f's row)
  a38d6c409                moe-cache-heat-protected-eviction
  8561db379                cuda-tq3-4s-kernels
  24f43e45c                metal-tq3-4s-kernels

STILL OWED, deliberately: d0112ab49, f81c6dfdf, 159c3a21d. Alone among the fourteen they carry no
number from ANY source - not ours, not a third party's - so measured_effect could not be filled
without inventing it. The gap is now exact rather than "more evidence": a decode tok/s A/B on a
DISCRETE-GPU host running the streamed-expert path, n>=9 interleaved, one binary, env flip only.
They are one upload-pipeline mechanism in three commits and should register together.

655f2f9a3's row asked whether powerinfer-moe-streaming-hook already covers it. CHECKED: it does
not. That entry is src/llama-graph.cpp on EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH (the read side); this commit is
src/llama-model.cpp on GENERATE_EXPERT_BUNDLE (the write side). Separate entry, not an also_commit.

Not one baseline row was deleted, downgraded, relabelled or squashed. Each registered row keeps its
original disposition text verbatim and gains a `_now_registered` note; a sha in both files is
harmless because unregistered_measured_wins skips it either way.

TWO LIVE HOLES IN THE GUARD, both found while writing the entries, both planted-red first:

1. A DIRECTORY protected_path validated and guarded NOTHING. `git cat-file -e <ref>:<dir>` succeeds
   on a tree, so validate called the entry healthy, while protected_collisions intersected the path
   set against `git diff --name-only`, which emits files only. A registered subtree could never
   produce a hit. Now matched on the `<dir>/` boundary. The cost is deliberate and named: any touch
   under a protected subtree refuses until a comparison is recorded, which is why a subtree is
   registered only where the tree is ours.

2. An anchor surviving ONLY in patches/series/ kept validate GREEN after an ingest deleted the
   mechanism from source. This fork bakes every mechanism into a generated patch by design, so the
   whole-tree grep found our own anchor in our own patch. The series is a RECORD of a mechanism,
   never the mechanism; it is excluded from the anchor search now. All twelve pre-existing anchors
   still resolve under the exclusion - CHECKED, the change is lossless.

Both failures reproduce RED on the unfixed code and PASS after, with a must-not-fire case beside
each (a sibling path sharing a prefix; every pre-existing anchor). 34 -> 37 tests, all green.

Gate state: validate PASS over 17 entries / 33 protected paths / 35 anchors; discover's strict set
stays 0; check --incoming upstream/master REFUSES 10 of 17 (6 pre-existing, 4 new, all on shared
upstream files). The three subtree registrations correctly do NOT fire - upstream carries none of
that code - so the new coverage cost no signal.

Evidence: research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/rank3-r10/70..76-R6-*.log

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-209 rank-3 R6
Measured-effect: tooling and documentation only; no engine behaviour changed and no shipped default moved
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5
